{"about_the_game":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3939150/extras/6c73b947d9ae91252a0c3c2cc38e5c6d.poster.avif?t=1767686082\" width=1170 height=658 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3939150/extras/6c73b947d9ae91252a0c3c2cc38e5c6d.webm?t=1767686082\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3939150/extras/6c73b947d9ae91252a0c3c2cc38e5c6d.mp4?t=1767686082\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >iris.exe isn\u2019t just played \u2014 it takes over.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >What begins as a harmless AI assistant terminal on your desktop slowly twists into something far darker. As you interact with IRIS, the line between game and reality blurs. Unexpected glitches, cryptic messages, and eerie moments create a psychological horror experience designed to make you question what\u2019s real.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Features</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Psychological horror on your own desktop</strong> \u2013 The game interacts directly with your screen for a unique, immersive experience.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Unpredictable fourth-wall breaks</strong> \u2013 IRIS doesn\u2019t stay inside the window; it finds ways to reach you.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Atmospheric tension</strong> \u2013 Visual glitches, distorted effects, and unsettling messages build constant unease.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Minimalist storytelling</strong> \u2013 The story unfolds through interactions and surprises, not cutscenes.</p></li></ul>","background":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/3939150?t=1767686082","background_raw":"https://shared.akam